  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue clan elders put Xiong Village among rival mountain clans that have produced talented juniors in recent years.",
      "chapters": [
        1
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The house name is 熊家 (Xiong House); Xiong is the word for bear.",
      "chapters": [
        22
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qing Mao Mountain holds three mountain villages. Gu Yue village sits at the mountain waist, the Xiong family village on the fore mountain, and the Bai family village at the back mountain waterfall.",
      "chapters": [
        65
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "loc_gu_yue_village",
        "loc_bai_village"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Bo later frames outside work as dealing with an arrogant and rude Xiong clan village alongside a gradually rising Bai clan village, and that wording treats the settlement as a Xiong clan village.",
      "chapters": [
        78
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_bo",
        "fac_xiong_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xiong village’s bear gall wine is named with Gu Yue’s green bamboo wine and Bai village’s white grain liquid as the three wines of Qing Mao.",
      "chapters": [
        117
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Xiong Li leads a five-person Xiong village special envoy toward Gu Yue village with a clan-head letter and orders to investigate the River Swallowing Toad matter, while warning his group not to degrade Xiong village prestige on Gu Yue ground. Bai village’s rise has broken the old Qing Mao balance, with Gu Yue weakened and Xiong village’s operations not running properly. Xiong Lin travels in that envoy party as that year’s top genius of Xiong village.",
      "chapters": [
        121
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "envoys-and-mountain-balance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiong_li",
        "gu_river_swallowing_toad",
        "char_xiong_lin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When a new thunder crown wolf pack reaches Gu Yue and Bai ground, elders guess it is the same force that attacked Xiong village, and some curse Xiong village for failing to hold even one wave. A lightning lycan is the true commander of that pack, and with that army of lightning wolves it is no wonder the Xiong clan was exterminated by them.",
      "chapters": [
        168
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-crisis",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later Gu Yue talk still treats Xiong clan as eliminated, then has to reverse that when an Xiong envoy arrives: Xiong clan still has a large number of survivors who retreated using a Gu their ancestor left behind and concealed many people. Gu Yue planning after that turn treats stealing the spirit spring as the prize if Xiong strength proves weak enough to crush.",
      "chapters": [
        175
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "survivors-and-gu-yue-plans",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qing Mao Mountain has only three spirit springs, and each is occupied by one of the three clans, so the Xiong seat holds one of those springs. After compensation talks fail, the three sides decide on a three-clan competition, with Xiong village able to preserve most of its strength.",
      "chapters": [
        180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "three-clan-competition",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_spirit_spring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the later crisis on Qing Mao Mountain, the mountain has already turned into a desolate ice mountain, and the three great clans along with countless living beings have all been frozen and will die within three to five days.",
      "chapters": [
        199
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
